English Translation (informational; the Chinese version governs)
========================================================================

1. Definitions
- "The Software" means the entire contents of this repository: SKILL.md,
  references/, scripts/, assets/, docs/, README, config and manifest files,
  together with all modifications and derivative works thereof.
- "Output" means content produced by *running or using* the Software (or a
  derivative): HTML posters, PNG / GIF / MP4 / PDF, vector files (SVG/EPS/AI),
  and resulting typesetting/copy deliverables.

2. Grant
Any person or organization is free of charge to use, study, copy, modify,
merge, translate and redistribute the Software, and to run it for any lawful
purpose including commercial internal use — subject to Sections 4 and 5.

3. Output belongs to the user: commercial use allowed, no copyleft duty
1. Content produced by using the Software belongs to the user, and may be
   used commercially, kept closed, re-licensed, or sold outright. This
   License requires neither open-sourcing nor attribution for Output.
2. Bundled third-party assets (fonts, icons, illustrations, vendor libraries)
   are neither "Output" nor re-licensed by this License; verify their own
   terms when shipping them.

4. Copyleft: copies and derivatives must stay open under this License
1. Redistribution of the Software (in whole or in substantial part), with or
   without modification, in source or packaged form, must be licensed
   entirely under this License (ACL-1.0) — no looser or stricter substitute;
2. Complete corresponding source must accompany redistribution, together
   with the copyright notice, this License text, and the upstream repo link;
3. Merging the Software or a derivative into another product / skill
   library / project and redistributing it requires that the portions
   containing derivative content be open-sourced under this License, with
   no license fee charged on them;
4. Offering the Software's functionality over a network (e.g. wrapped as an
   online tool, SaaS, API, or hosted skill) counts as redistribution:
   complete corresponding source must be made available to service users.

5. No resale of the Software itself
1. The Software itself (or copies/derivatives of it) must not be sold,
   rented, or offered on a subscription basis as a standalone product, nor
   charged for as a "license fee";
2. The following are expressly NOT resale and are allowed:
   a. Charging distribution cost (media, shipping, bandwidth) — the Software
      itself must remain unpriced;
   b. Charging for installation, customization, training, or consulting;
   c. **Selling Output created with the Software** (finished designs,
      collateral packages, production services).

6. No Warranty
THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
LIABILITY ARISING FROM THE SOFTWARE.
